00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:36,980
<v KAEDEN> Hello Charlotte, I'm Caden, one of the supervisors.

00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,400
<v KAEDEN> Welcome to the team.

00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:39,660
<v CHARLOTTE> Hi Aidan.

00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,360
<v KAEDEN> It's Caden.

00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:42,880
<v CHARLOTTE> I'm so sorry.

00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,540
<v KAEDEN> Don't worry, people often get my name wrong.

00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:47,820
<v KAEDEN> They never know how to spell it.

00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:54,280
<v KAEDEN> It's K-A-E-D-E-N, in case you ever need to write it.

00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:56,120
<v CHARLOTTE> I'll try and remember.

00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:01,560
<v KAEDEN> So, there are a few practical things you need to sort out this morning.

00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:04,280
<v KAEDEN> Then I'll show you what you're going to do today.

00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:11,980
<v CHARLOTTE> The email I received said to go to the front desk to show my letter of appointment and pick up my badge.

00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:17,680
<v KAEDEN> You'll need that for the staff room and other areas of the supermarket where shoppers aren't allowed.

00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:23,040
<v KAEDEN> So, after you've finished at the front desk, I'll take you to the staff room.

00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:26,320
<v KAEDEN> Put your coat and rucksack in one of the lockers there.

00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:28,400
<v KAEDEN> Take whichever one is free.

00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,220
<v CHARLOTTE> Will I have a key?

00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:31,420
<v KAEDEN> Yes.

00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:32,940
<v KAEDEN> Try not to lose it.

00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:37,160
<v KAEDEN> At the end of the day, leave it in the door for the next person to use.

00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,120
<v CHARLOTTE> Will do.

00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:42,180
<v KAEDEN> You also need to go to the HR department to see Tiffany.

00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:43,660
<v KAEDEN> She's really helpful.

00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:47,020
<v CHARLOTTE> I was told to bring my passport with me.

00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,140
<v CHARLOTTE> HR need to take a note of the number in it.

00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,020
<v KAEDEN> That's right.

00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,940
<v KAEDEN> Or you can show your ID card.

00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,760
<v CHARLOTTE> I don't have one of those.

00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,360
<v KAEDEN> OK.

00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:57,420
<v KAEDEN> Tiffany will give you a uniform.

00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:01,880
<v KAEDEN> They have lots in different sizes, so you just tell her what you need.

00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,760
<v KAEDEN> I won't come with you to HR.

00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,980
<v KAEDEN> I've got to go and sort something else out.

00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,540
<v KAEDEN> Um, problem with a bread slicer.

00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,780
<v CHARLOTTE> Is the HR office near the staff room?

00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:17,600
<v KAEDEN> The staff room's on the first floor and HR are a couple of floors above that, on the third floor.

00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,380
<v KAEDEN> There's a staircase outside the staff room.

00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,080
<v CHARLOTTE> OK.

00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:25,620
<v KAEDEN> When you've finished with HR, come and find me in the bakery section of the shop.

00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,320
<v CHARLOTTE> I'm looking forward to getting started.

00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,260
<v KAEDEN> I'll just give you my phone number in case you can't find me.

00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,320
<v KAEDEN> Have you got your phone there?

00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:35,600
<v CHARLOTTE> Yes.

00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:36,740
<v CHARLOTTE> OK.

00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:37,900
<v CHARLOTTE> Ready.

00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:45,160
<v KAEDEN> It's 0412 665903.

00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:46,500
<v CHARLOTTE> OK.

00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:47,420
<v CHARLOTTE> Done.

00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:33,270
<v KAEDEN> So, Charlotte, your tasks today are in the bakery section, on the sushi counter and on the meat and fish counters.

<v KAEDEN> 00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:38,010
<v CHARLOTTE> The first job is to check sell-by dates on the bread and cakes.

00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:42,550
<v KAEDEN> If any of the dates are today's, put a new price label on the packaging.

00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:47,470
<v CHARLOTTE> What if any of the labels are yesterday's dates or older?

00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:49,970
<v CHARLOTTE> Do I throw those items away?

00:04:50,430 --> 00:04:51,950
<v KAEDEN> Yes, but that shouldn't happen.

00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:53,490
<v KAEDEN> We check the stock every day.

00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:59,250
<v KAEDEN> When something needs a new price label, put a yellow one on the package, next to the original price.

00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:00,050
<v CHARLOTTE> OK.

00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:03,790
<v KAEDEN> After that, you'll go to the sushi takeaway counter.

00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:06,950
<v CHARLOTTE> Will I be preparing boxes of food?

00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:09,950
<v KAEDEN> For today, you'll just be helping the staff.

00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,110
<v CHARLOTTE> Yes, of course.

00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:15,070
<v KAEDEN> You'll see lots of flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter.

00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:18,410
<v KAEDEN> Beneath those is where we keep the plastic boxes.

00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:22,990
<v KAEDEN> We run out of those really quickly, so you should bring more from the storeroom.

00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:26,310
<v CHARLOTTE> Is that my only task on the sushi counter?

00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:27,290
<v KAEDEN> No.

00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:30,230
<v KAEDEN> You also need to clean the area where they prepare the dishes.

00:05:30,810 --> 00:05:33,090
<v KAEDEN> There are cloths and bottles of spray by the sink.

00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:36,010
<v KAEDEN> Oh, and please make sure you clean that, too.

00:05:36,350 --> 00:05:36,770
<v CHARLOTTE> Sure.

00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:38,730
<v CHARLOTTE> That's important, isn't it?

00:05:38,730 --> 00:05:39,530
<v KAEDEN> Absolutely.

00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:41,530
<v KAEDEN> But you mustn't wash up knives.

00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:45,390
<v KAEDEN> You have to do some training before you're allowed to touch sharp objects.

00:05:45,850 --> 00:05:47,890
<v CHARLOTTE> What should I do if there are any?

00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:50,010
<v KAEDEN> Ask someone to put them in the dishwasher.

00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:51,490
<v CHARLOTTE> OK, thanks.

00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:53,570
<v CHARLOTTE> I don't want to get anything wrong.

00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:55,150
<v KAEDEN> Don't worry, you'll be fine.

00:05:55,590 --> 00:05:56,710
<v KAEDEN> And I'll be around to help.

00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:57,310
<v CHARLOTTE> Right.

00:05:58,370 --> 00:06:00,330
<v KAEDEN> Finally, the meat and fish counters.

00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:06,110
<v KAEDEN> You need to clean the area where staff serve customers, including wiping the weighing scales.

00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:06,790
<v CHARLOTTE> OK.

00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:08,850
<v CHARLOTTE> Anything else?

00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:15,030
<v KAEDEN> The fish is laid on ice, but when that starts to melt, you'll need to get more from the cold room.

00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:19,270
<v CHARLOTTE> I know the staff on the food counters wear a hat.

00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:21,350
<v CHARLOTTE> Will that be the same for me?

00:06:21,810 --> 00:06:24,430
<v KAEDEN> You won't be serving customers directly, so no.

00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:28,870
<v KAEDEN> But make sure you put on thermal gloves when you take anything out of the cold room.

00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:32,650
<v KAEDEN> The temperature's low enough in there to get frostbite from touching things.

00:06:33,110 --> 00:06:33,590
<v CHARLOTTE> Understood.